0..42 Comment "/// A derived filler owes a model nothing."
43..46 Comment "///"
47..115 Comment "/// Completion derives the associator of four from a monoid\'s binary"
116..191 Comment "/// associativity and proves it for every model. So a model writes only its"
192..213 Comment "/// rules\' witnesses."
214..217 Comment "///"
218..294 Comment "/// The derived rule declaration states the associator, and a model reads it"
295..371 Comment "/// as the theory\'s member `Monoid.assoc4`. Both sides rewrite to one normal"
372..413 Comment "/// form, and the rewrites are the proof."
414..417 Comment "///"
418..497 Comment "/// - see: #4106 — a component a model writes for a derived filler is refused"
498..576 Comment "/// - see: `pathological/identity/derived-associator.gandr` — the model that"
577..608 Comment "///   writes the associator too"
609..683 Comment "/// - see: Knuth and Bendix, _Simple Word Problems in Universal Algebras_,"
684..715 Comment "///   1970, § 7 — completion"
717..773 Comment "/// A monoid\'s unit and associativity laws, each a rule."
